# =============================================================================
# StockPilot — environment templates
# =============================================================================
#
# Self-hosted Docker + second PC: see docs/SECOND_PC.md (standalone first; cloud optional).
# Template for Docker Compose root `.env`: `.env.docker.example` — filled by `npm run generate:docker-env`.
#
#
# The app reads VITE_* variables from Vite "modes" (see README → Local vs cloud).
#
# DO NOT put VITE_SUPABASE_URL / VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in `.env.local` if you use
# `npm run dev` or `npm run dev:cloud` — those keys would override mode files and
# break switching. Keep cloud Supabase keys in `.env.cloud.local` only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev (default): `npm run dev` or `npm run dev:local`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uses `.env.development` (committed local Supabase defaults) for `npm run dev`.
# Optional: `.env.development.local` (gitignored) overrides the same variable names.
# After `npx supabase db reset`, sign in with username `admin` / password `devpass123` (local only; see README).
# After `npx supabase start`, if auth fails, run `npx supabase status -o env` and update
# `VITE_SUPABASE_*` in `.env.development` or put overrides in `.env.development.local`.
#
# Admin → Data sync (local ↔ hosted) while using `npm run dev`:
# Option A — add to `.env.development` OR `.env.development.local`:
#   VITE_SYNC_CLOUD_URL=https://your-ref.supabase.co
#   VITE_SYNC_CLOUD_ANON_KEY=your-hosted-anon-key
# Option B — reuse hosted `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` + `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` from `.env.cloud.local`
#   (Vite merges that file in development for sync; restart `npm run dev` after edits).
# The sync page signs in to the hosted project with email/password (session not persisted).
# Use the exact email from that hosted project: Authentication → Users (e.g. admin@members.stockpilot.local),
# not the short username from the main app login unless that literal email exists on hosted.
# Prefer `.env.development.local` for hosted secrets if `.env.development` is committed to git.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud dev: `npm run dev:cloud`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy `.env.cloud.example` → `.env.cloud.local` and set real URL + anon key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production build: `npm run build` (mode: production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` in CI or use gitignored
# `.env.production.local` for local production builds. Vercel: Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB migrations to hosted Supabase (unchanged)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional in `.env.local` only (not loaded by Vite for the SPA):
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=your-database-password
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...   (session pooler URI from Dashboard → Connect)
# SUPABASE_POOLER_REGION=eu-west-1
# Optional for Supabase CLI (link, etc.): SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=...  (never commit; file is gitignored)
#
# Then: `npm run db:push:local`
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mirror hosted Auth → local (script only; never use service role in the SPA)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# **Use this when operators/members must match hosted Auth** (same user ids) on a shop PC
# running **Docker Compose** (`docker-compose.yml`) or CLI `supabase start`.
#
# Copy [`.env.mirror-auth.example`](./.env.mirror-auth.example) → `.env.mirror-auth.local` and fill:
#   MIRROR_CLOUD_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_REF.supabase.co
#   MIRROR_CLOUD_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # Dashboard → Settings → API → service_role
#   MIRROR_LOCAL_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000   # Kong on **this** PC (Docker self-hosted)
#     (or `http://127.0.0.1:54321` for `npx supabase start` only)
#   MIRROR_LOCAL_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # Docker: `SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in root `.env`; CLI: `npx supabase status -o env`
# Optional:
#   MIRROR_LOCAL_PASSWORD=devpass123         # applied to every mirrored user (min 8 chars)
# Run:
#   npm run mirror:cloud-auth-to-local -- --dry-run
#   I_CONFIRM_WIPE_LOCAL_AUTH=YES npm run mirror:cloud-auth-to-local
# Then run **Admin → Data sync** once. See README → Admin data sync → "Mirror hosted Auth onto local".
